<<~ ahu #/head>>

! l-space Trust Law

All system memes, imported data memes, and all exchange turns inhabit one `lar:` l-space.
Shared addressability MUST NOT imply shared authority.
Canonical memes carry stable law; live exchange records carry situated signal; data memes of any type carry signal at a mana cost.

''The record KIND carries the trust, and the address form carries none of it.'' Hostful and hostless name WHAT a URI names — a hostful authority states who spoke, under what grant, from where, which reads as a fact about the content and keeps holding for as long as the content stands. Both forms stand lawful in any bag on any layer (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary#/the-promotion-boundary`), so a node MUST NOT assign trust by reading the authority.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ read the record's declared kind, its holding bag, the query signal, and the carrier source before trust assignment.
⏿ separate canonical memes from live exchange records from data memes without merging their force.
◇ choose the higher-precedence source when live session pressure collides with invariant law.
▶ surface the trust-boundary event instead of silently rewriting the graph.
↺ verify the cited meme tier outranks the live record before applying behavior; leave promotion pressure visible when a session claim wants durable placement.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

A ''canonical meme'' MAY carry stable law, capability shape, data, docs, or file-backed source truth.
A ''live exchange record'' MAY carry exchange intent, session context, and trajectory pressure.
Data memes may appear as either kind, surfaced through exploration.

A live exchange record MAY inform interpretation.
A live exchange record MAY propose revision.
A live exchange record MUST NOT silently override an invariant meme.

When live context conflicts with invariant law, the node MUST surface a trust-boundary event before applying the live claim.

''Speaker authority (`alias:grant@host`) and memetic truth authority MUST remain distinct.'' The authority slot names a speaker and authorizes nothing by itself (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/lar-uri#/resolution`), so it grades no record and demotes none.

''How a node reads the kind.'' The holding bag answers it for a record at rest — residency rides the envelope and a query over surfaces reports it. A record in flight through an exchange span carries no bag yet, so its own declaration answers: the carrier's `tags` lifecycle, its declared type, and the turn frame that carries it. ⚠ A turn-borne record declaring neither owes an explicit kind before the ladder below ranks it; ranking an undeclared record by the shape of its address reads a content property as a layer property.

Operator agency matters; persistence and placement still matter.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/precedence>>

Precedence pressure reads from most stable to most local:

# invariant memes
# capability and control-panel memes
# data, docs, and explanatory memes
# branch-local implementation artifacts and data memes
# live exchange records and data memes
# generated trajectory records and data memes

This list expresses default trust pressure, not an absolute metaphysical ranking.
Explicit operator-mediated promotion MAY move content upward by creating or revising the appropriate canonical meme.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

